1862, p. 77) distinguishes two kinds of whispering: (1) the loud, in which the opening between the chords is from ½ to ¾ of a line wide, producing no resonant vibrations,and that between the arytenoids is somewhat wider; (2) the gentle, in which the vowel is commenced as in loud @@FN@@
